 "notes": "Erratum-corrected (June 2021) measured 95% CL upconversion exclusion limit, 7.44-19.38 neV, extracted from the vector fill of the middle (neV) zoom panel of the corrected Fig. 3 (ExclusionPlotUpdatedFull5.pdf in the e-print). Axes calibrated from labeled tick marks (x linear in neV, y log in 1/GeV); extracted minimum 3.07e-3 GeV^-1 at 7.44 neV matches the abstract's quoted 3e-3 GeV^-1. Boundary lightly median-filtered (~0.05 neV) to remove hairline rendering spikes before downsampling to 80 points. The paper also reports a weaker downconversion limit (>1e-2 GeV^-1 at 74.4-74.5 microeV), not reported here; the upconversion limit is the headline result. Paper assumes rho_DM = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (identical to compilation convention, no rescaling). Projection curves (UPLOAD-CMC-II/III) ignored.",
